  "configuration_id": "config_032",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only multiprofile with scvi_n200 is the clear best configuration so far (config_005/006: ~0.65 acc), with transformer and avgpool being nearly equivalent. Image-only resnet50 is very weak (0.208), raising uncertainty about whether adding image in a multimodal setting will help or dilute the strong RNA signal. Question: Does adding resnet50 image features (concat fusion) to the best RNA-only multiprofile scvi_n200 transformer configuration improve or degrade performance? This directly tests the value of multimodality against the current best baseline (config_006, 0.653) with only one variable changed (adding image + concat). Why best use of budget: All completed experiments are unimodal; the central open question is whether multimodal fusion adds value at all. Testing with the already-characterized resnet50 encoder and the simplest fusion (concat) isolates the multimodal question cleanly. If it helps, we can then explore better image encoders or fusion strategies; if it hurts, we save budget by not pursuing multimodal further."
}

